<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shivaskandavarman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shivaskandavarman was one of the earliest known kings of the Pallava dynasty, ruling in the fourth century CE from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a>. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate charters in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prakrit">Prakrit</a>, such as the Mayidavolu and Hirahadagalli grants, record gifts of land in the Andhra country and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ballari">Bellary</a> region and claim that he performed great Vedic sacrifices, including the horse sacrifice.</p></div>
